WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.009
It's been a long time since Mike Myers took
us on a groovy journey through time and espionage

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:09.610
with his Austin Powers franchise, a three-film
romp that featured a star-studded cast of

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.700
past and future celebrities.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.390
In the decades since, some of these actors
have hung onto their mojo, while others are

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.800
resting on their laurels.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.340
Here's a look back at where the cast was before
the films, and where they are now.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.220
Mike Myers

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.039
Before he played Austin Powers, Dr. Evil,
and the endlessly hungry Fat Bastard, Mike

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:32.110
Myers played a slew of characters during his
six-year run on Saturday Night Live — including

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:36.620
metalhead Wayne Campbell, who of course appeared
in his own feature film franchise.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.660
Once the Austin Powers trilogy ended, Myers
went on to voice the beloved title character

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:41.920
in the Shrek franchise.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.340
But sadly, his other work wasn't as well-received;
2008's The Love Guru won a terrible trifecta

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.800
of Razzie Awards for Worst Actor, Worst Screenplay,
and Worst Picture—plus a nomination for

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.700
Myers for Worst Actor of the Decade.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.240
"Ouch baby, very ouch."

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:04.290
Still, Myers has left his mark on Hollywood:
his Walk of Fame star was unveiled in 2002,

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:08.840
and in his home country of Canada, he's a
national hero with his own commemorative stamp.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.170
And if you're more likely to see him at a
Toronto Maple Leafs game than on the big screen

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:16.420
these days, it might be because the Austin
Powers and Shrek franchises combined made

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.360
him even wealthier than Dr. Evil.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.520
Elizabeth Hurley

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.920
This English actress is probably best known
for her role as Vanessa Kensington in the

00:01:25.931 --> 00:01:30.430
first two Austin Powers films, but those are
just a pair of entries in a lengthy filmography

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:34.900
that includes movies like Rowing with the
Wind and Bedazzled, where she plays a smoking

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.500
hot devil.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.620
And offscreen, Hurley is famous in her own
right for her modeling work — and by association

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.320
for her 13-year relationship with Hugh Grant,
standing by him during the 1995 scandal in

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.500
which Grant after being caught with a Hollywood
prostitute.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.960
"I did a bad thing, and there you have it."

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.420
These days, Hurley is flying solo and staying
busy — running a beachwear company and playing

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.240
Queen Helena on the E! television series The
Royals.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:58.800
Michael York

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.660
Long before Austin Powers hit theaters, the
English actor who plays Basil Exposition was

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.560
a veteran of stage and screen since the mid-1960s,
starring in films like The Taming of the Shrew

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.240
and Romeo and Juliet, and on Broadway in the
original production of Tennessee Williams'

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:12.760
Out Cry.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.360
And don't even get us started on his television
credits.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.340
York reprised his role for all three Austin
Powers films, but since 2010, the actor has

00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:25.421
rarely been seen onscreen — and has been
undergoing treatment for amyloidosis, a rare

00:02:25.421 --> 00:02:29.660
medical condition caused by the abnormal production
of insoluble proteins in the body.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.500
Mimi Rogers

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.650
Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery
is merely a side note on the resume of this

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:41.040
actress, producer and competitive poker player,
who famously starred in the 1991 religious

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.300
drama The Rapture.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.380
After the first Austin Powers movie, Rogers
went on to appear in films like Lost in Space

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:51.300
and Ginger Snaps, and on popular television
shows including The X-Files and Mad Men.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:52.920
Robert Wagner

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.879
Long before he starred as Dr. Evil's right-hand
man, Robert Wagner was one of the hardest

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.640
working actors in Hollywood.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.480
"Who does number two work for?"

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.260
Who does number two work for?

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.260
Pretty much everyone!

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:12.040
Wagner's starring roles include TV shows like
It Takes a Thief, Switch, and Hart to Hart

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.520
— and in the twenty-first century, you could
find him on Two and a Half Men and NCIS.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.849
But Wagner might be most famous for his role
in one of classic Hollywood's biggest tragedies.

00:03:21.849 --> 00:03:26.820
In 1981, Wagner's Oscar-nominated wife Natalie
Wood drowned while sailing off the coast of

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.780
California with Wagner and actor Christopher
Walken.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.879
Wood's death was ruled an accident, but lingering
questions about the possibility of foul play

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:39.430
resulted in the investigation being re-opened
in 2013, with the Los Angeles coroner's office

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.750
amending the actress' cause of death to include
"undetermined factors".

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:46.709
The decision to reopen the investigation was
supported by Wagner, who's still mourning

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:48.980
his wife's death more than thirty years later.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:55.960
"I don't think you ever overcome it - and
why should you?"

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.860
Seth Green

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.640
After he played Dr. Evil's son Scott in all
three Austin Powers movies, Hollywood was

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.240
only too happy to throw a frickin' bone to
Seth Green.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.040
Twenty years after he refused to hug his evil
dad onscreen, Green has found massive success

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:16.960
as the creator (and producer, writer, director,
and main vocal talent) of Adult Swim's stop-motion

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.120
sketch comedy show Robot Chicken.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:23.720
Green was also a staple of comedies like Can't
Hardly Wait and Without a Paddle, and he's

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.740
been heard but not seen as the voice of Family
Guy's Chris Griffin.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.720
"Stop it!"

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.220
"Ahhh!"

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.360
"My hat!"

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.360
"Haha.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.280
Wear it NOW!"

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.620
And with various prestigious awards under
his belt for his work on Robot Chicken, this

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.560
is one Austin Powers star who hasn't lost
his mojo since 1997.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.690
Mindy Sterling

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.810
Although Sterling got her start playing with
puppets on the children's TV series Dusty's

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:52.660
Treehouse, it's her role as Dr. Evil's associate
Frau Farbissina where she truly made her mark

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.260
on Hollywood's hearts… and eardrums.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:56.800
"SCOTT!"

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:01.380
So you probably won't recognize Sterling from
anywhere else—unless you watch TV with your

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:01.960
kids.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:06.620
Despite her street cred as Evil's girl Friday,
the actress is a popular casting pick on Disney,

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.380
Nickelodeon, and other children's networks,
where her comedy credentials definitely make

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:12.980
her well-suited for family-friendly roles.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:14.540
Will Ferrell

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.780
After notching his big-screen breakthrough
in Austin Powers: The Spy Who Shagged Me,

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.380
Mike Myers' fellow SNL veteran became a comedy
star in his own right, bringing laughs in

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.630
films like Old School, Anchorman, and Talladega
Nights.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:30.180
"Here's the deal, I'm the best there is, plain
and simple…

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.060
I mean, I wake up in the morning and I p-ss
excellence."

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.160
Ferrell also had one of the most memorable
runs in Saturday Night Live history, where

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:40.920
he became famous for impersonating famous
figures like George W. Bush, Cubs announcer

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:43.770
Harry Caray, and Jeopardy! host Alex Trebek.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:48.130
Nowadays, he's still making movies — and
making fun of himself, often to earn money

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:52.530
for charitable causes, as with his "10 Major
League Baseball Teams in One Day" stunt from

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:53.500
2015.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.140
Heather Graham

00:05:55.640 --> 00:06:00.180
Way before she played Felicity Shagwell in
the Austin Powers sequel, Heather Graham broke

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:05.300
out in Hollywood in the late 1980s with License
to Drive, followed by Twin Peaks and Boogie

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.300
Nights.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.820
And after traveling back to 1969 for The Spy
Who Shagged Me, Graham didn't slow down

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.900
After playing Felicity Shagwell, Graham went
on to star in films like Committed, Say It

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:18.320
Isn't So, and the Hangover series, and more
recently, she's been featured in recurring

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:22.400
roles on series like Showtime's Californication
and Netflix's Flaked.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.800
"I'm pretty enough to be on TV, right?"

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:26.260
Beyoncé

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:31.620
Unless you've been living under a rock, this
is one Austin Powers alumna who needs no introduction.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:36.800
The 22-time Grammy Award winner is one of
America's Top 50 Richest Self-Made Women,

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:41.330
with more than 100 million records sold worldwide
— and that's just her solo career.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:45.890
But the majority of Beyoncé's success came
after she played the leading lady Foxxy Cleopatra

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:50.140
in Austin Powers in Goldmember, even if she
was already well on her way to superstardom

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:52.380
by then as the lead singer of Destiny's Child.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.060
Michael Caine

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:59.160
This icon of the British screen has been acting
since the 1950s, and he was an Oscar nominee

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.780
long before he played Austin Powers' father
in Goldmember.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:06.470
Caine worked steadily throughout the 1970s
and 80s, starring in films like Get Carter

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:10.600
and Woody Allen's Hannah and Her Sisters,
for which he earned the first of two Academy

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.060
Awards for Best Supporting Actor.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.960
But since he showed the world where Austin
got his groove, Caine is probably best known

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:20.210
for his work with director Christopher Nolan
— particularly in his role as Alfred Pennyworth

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.460
in the Dark Knight trilogy, where, as Nolan's
favorite cast member, he had all the best

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:24.980
lines.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.400
"Some men just want to watch the world burn."

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.040
Verne Troyer

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:34.460
Though he's best known for playing the miniature
clone of Dr. Evil, Verne Troyer has a big

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.540
presence in Hollywood.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:39.930
The 2 feet 8 inch tall actor has brought his
unique stature to films like Pinocchio's Revenge

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.780
and Mighty Joe Young — and he was the first
to play Griphook the goblin in Harry Potter

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:47.860
and the Sorcerer's Stone, though he was replaced
in later films by fellow actor and friend

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:48.900
Warwick Davis.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.860
Troyer also maintains an active social media
presence, where he's recently admitted to

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.900
battling alcohol addiction and thanked his
fans for their support.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:57.640
Fred Savage

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.200
"So you're the…

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.400
MO…

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.100
MO...

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:07.400
Apart from this bit as a spy with a prominent mole in Goldmember, there's one role that

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.690
will follow Fred Savage for the rest of his
life.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:13.280
Of course, we're talking about The Wonder
Years, where the young actor earned two Golden

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:17.440
Globe nominations and two Emmy nominations
for playing the lead role of Kevin Arnold

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:22.310
— although yes, that's also him in The Princess
Bride, giving the stink-eye to all things

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:22.840
romantic:

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.060
"Is this a kissing book?"

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:29.220
After his role in the Austin Powers franchise,
Savage moved on mostly to voice acting, with

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:33.620
appearances on Family Guy, Kim Possible, and
BoJack Horseman, and he's kept busy behind

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:34.980
the camera as a TV director.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.460
But if you're dying to see his face onscreen
— without that mole in the way — he's

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:42.740
also getting back into acting, with starring
roles in both seasons of The Grinder and the

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:44.520
Netflix series Friends from College.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:45.920
Thanks for watching!

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:48.040
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.080
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

